            <ArticleTitle>Practical guide to laparoscopic pain mapping.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>8-11</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jmig.2009.10.008</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Conscious laparoscopic pain mapping, a technique that has been described in the literature for more than a decade, can be a particularly helpful tool to assist with pelvic pain diagnosis and treatment decisions. Several factors, when optimized, increase the likelihood of a good outcome. Herein, we review the literature and address common questions about pain mapping including appropriate patient selection, standard technique, typical outcomes, and how the results might influence treatment.</AbstractText>
